---
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout title="About Me" date={new Date('November 14 1998')} tags={[]} slug="about">
	<p>
		I'm a physicist who fell into software engineering and never looked back. I studied Physics at
		Universidad Nacional de Colombia before realizing the problem-solving itself was what I loved,
		not the physics lab specifically. Today I'm a Software Engineer at Nubank, building backend
		platforms in Clojure — a language that rewards thinking clearly about a system before you touch
		it, the same way physics does.
	</p>
	<p>
		Quantum computing is where the two still meet. Between the Qiskit Global Summer School, IBM's
		Quantum Challenge (Fall 2021, Advanced track), and being an IBM Certified Associate Developer for
		Quantum Computation using Qiskit, it's the one field where I get to use both halves of what I
		studied.
	</p>
	<p>
		Outside of work: I'd rather document the learning than just get to the answer, which is why this
		blog exists — generated straight from my own org-roam notes. I tinker with electronics, play
		guitar badly but happily (rock and blues), and I'm stubborn about finishing what I start. My <a
			href="https://github.com/diegoherrera262"
			target="_blank">GitHub</a
		> is the most honest record of all of it.
	</p>

	<h2>Where I've been</h2>
	<Timeline />
</Layout>
